ree):\n","    response = ask_llm(\"Where is my order right now?\")\n","\n","# Finish the parent run\n","run_tree.end(outputs={\"response\": response})\n","run_tree.patch()\n","\n","# print(\"Response:\", response)\n","print(\"Trace ID:\", run_tree.id)\n","print(\"Name:\", run_tree.name)\n","print(\"Run Type:\", run_tree.run_type)\n","print(\"Inputs:\", run_tree.inputs)\n","print(\"Outputs:\", run_tree.outputs)\n","print(\"Start Time:\", run_tree.start_time)\n","print(\"End Time:\", run_tree.end_time)\n","print(\"Tags:\", run_tree.tags)\n","print(\"Metadata:\", run_tree.extra)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"03a3fbb9","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009055,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.245296+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.236241+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["What happens?\n","\n","![LangSmith LLM](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/langsmith_llm.png)\n","\n","LangSmith captures the execution of the traced function and supported nested LangChain operations.\n","\n","The SDK supports wrappers and decorators for capturing LLM calls.\n","\n","\n","One important point:\n","\n","> Tracing is not the same thing as changing the LLM response. LangSmith observes and records the application execution; it is not itself the model generating your answer."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"8f8d403c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.008863,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.26308+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.254217+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Dataset\n","\n","A dataset is a collection of test cases used to evaluate an AI application. A dataset is your benchmark.\n","\n","It typically contains:\n","\n","- Inputs.\n","- Reference outputs, when available.\n","- Optional metadata.\n","\n","The reference output is used by evaluators. It is not necessarily passed to the model during inference.\n","\n","LangSmith supports datasets, experiments, versioning, and comparisons."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":23,"id":"42283df6","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.282964Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.282379Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.28797Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.286969Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.017579,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.289881+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.272302+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["dataset_name = \"qa-evaluation-dataset\"\n","\n","data = [\n","    {\n","        \"question\": \"What is Python?\",\n","        \"expected_answer\": \"Python is a programming language.\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"question\": \"What is LangSmith?\",\n","        \"expected_answer\": \"LangSmith is a platform for debugging and evaluating LLM applications.\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"question\": \"What is RAG?\",\n","        \"expected_answer\": \"RAG stands for Retrieval Augmented Generation.\"\n","    }\n","]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":24,"id":"d7a41cdd","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.309345Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.308862Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.637372Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.636153Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.341254,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.640092+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.298838+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Uploaded 3/3\n","Dataset created successfully!\n"]}],"source":["# Create dataset if it doesn't exist\n","if not client.has_dataset(dataset_name=dataset_name):\n","    client.create_dataset(\n","        dataset_name=dataset_name,\n","        description=\"QA evaluation dataset\"\n","    )\n","\n","# Convert data into LangSmith format\n","examples = [\n","    {\n","        \"inputs\": {\n","            \"question\": item[\"question\"]\n","        },\n","        \"outputs\": {\n","            \"answer\": item[\"expected_answer\"]\n","        }\n","    }\n","    for item in data\n","]\n","\n","# Upload in batches\n","BATCH_SIZE = 100\n","\n","for i in range(0, len(examples), BATCH_SIZE):\n","\n","    batch = examples[i:i + BATCH_SIZE]\n","\n","    client.create_examples(\n","        dataset_name=dataset_name,\n","        examples=batch\n","    )\n","\n","    print(f\"Uploaded {min(i + BATCH_SIZE, len(examples))}/{len(examples)}\")\n","\n","print(\"Dataset created successfully!\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"0f5dfc72","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.011093,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.66384+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.652747+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["**Experiment**\n","\n","An experiment is the result of running a particular application version against a dataset.\n","\n","Suppose you compare three configurations:\n","\n","| Experiment   | Model        | Prompt    |\n","| ------------ | ------------ | --------- |\n","| Experiment A | Gemini Flash | Prompt V1 |\n","| Experiment B | Gemini Flash | Prompt V2 |\n","| Experiment C | GPT model    | Prompt V2 |\n","\n","Each experiment produces:\n","\n","- Model outputs.\n","- Execution traces.\n","- Evaluation scores.\n","- Performance data.\n","\n","You can compare the experiments side by side.\n","\n","The concepts are:\n","\n","![Dataset](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/langsmith_dataset.png)\n","\n","**Dataset Versioning**\n","\n","Suppose your dataset originally contains 100 test questions. Later, you add 20 more questions. Now you have 120 examples. If the benchmark silently changes, comparing older results against newer results can be misleading.\n","\n","LangSmith creates dataset versions as examples are changed, which helps you track how the benchmark evolves."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"d50b49f0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009101,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.682525+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.673424+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["\n","## LangSmith Evaluation\n","\n","Tracing tells you what happened. Evaluation tells you how good the result was. Suppose your chatbot answers 100 questions.\n","\n","You want to know:\n","\n","- How many answers are correct?\n","- How many answers are relevant?\n","- How many answers contain hallucinations?\n","- How many answers are grounded in retrieved documents?\n","- Which model performs better?\n","- Which prompt performs better?\n","\n","Evaluation helps measure those qualities systematically.\n","\n","**Evaluation approaches**\n","\n","1. **LLM-as-judge**: An LLM evaluates another model's answer.\n","2. **Code evaluator**: Rules and functions score outputs.\n","\n","\n","### Code-based evaluation"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":25,"id":"35a7eadd","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.701952Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.701621Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.709498Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.708284Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.020416,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.711649+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:13:07.691233+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def exact_match(run, example):\n","    outputs = run.outputs or {}\n","\n","    actual_answer = outputs.get(\"answer\", \"\").strip().lower()\n","\n","    expected_answer = example.outputs.get(\n","        \"expected_answer\", \"\"\n","    ).strip().lower()\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"key\": \"exact_match\",\n","        \"score\": actual_answer == expected_answer\n","    }\n","\n","def keyword_check(run, example):\n","    outputs = run.outputs or {}\n","\n","    answer = outputs.get(\"answer\", \"\").lower()\n","\n","    expected_answer = example.outputs.get(\n","  