"      <td>False</td>\n","      <td>False</td>\n","      <td>12.540985</td>\n","      <td>a47e8850-433b-4e06-b4e0-9a8321024e06</td>\n","      <td>01a1f8ea-e104-73e8-bb4f-f394753e7ccb</td>\n","    </tr>\n","    <tr>\n","      <th>32</th>\n","      <td>What is Python?</td>\n","      <td>**Python** is a high-level, general-purpose pr...</td>\n","      <td>None</td>\n","      <td>Python is a programming language.</td>\n","      <td>False</td>\n","      <td>False</td>\n","      <td>11.529514</td>\n","      <td>a8496bad-516d-43ba-b430-40d99a17e8f7</td>\n","      <td>01a1f8eb-1205-793e-bc44-466818c113cd</td>\n","    </tr>\n","  </tbody>\n","</table>\n","</div>"],"text/plain":["<ExperimentResults llm-judge-experiment-9ff7020a>"]},"execution_count":33,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["results"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":34,"id":"3902ba62","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.270345Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.269769Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.279275Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.278312Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.023611,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.281525+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.257914+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Total Questions: 33\n","\n","Exact Match Evaluation\n","Passed: 0\n","Failed: 33\n","Accuracy: 0.0 %\n","\n","Keyword Check Evaluation\n","Passed: 0\n","Failed: 33\n","Accuracy: 0.0 %\n"]}],"source":["df = results.to_pandas()\n","\n","total = len(df)\n","\n","exact_pass = df[\"feedback.exact_match\"].sum()\n","keyword_pass = df[\"feedback.keyword_check\"].sum()\n","\n","print(\"Total Questions:\", total)\n","\n","print(\"\\nExact Match Evaluation\")\n","print(\"Passed:\", exact_pass)\n","print(\"Failed:\", total - exact_pass)\n","print(\"Accuracy:\", round(exact_pass / total * 100, 2), \"%\")\n","\n","print(\"\\nKeyword Check Evaluation\")\n","print(\"Passed:\", keyword_pass)\n","print(\"Failed:\", total - keyword_pass)\n","print(\"Accuracy:\", round(keyword_pass / total * 100, 2), \"%\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"fcae471e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.01012,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.301028+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.290908+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Offline Evaluation vs Online Evaluation\n","\n","**Offline evaluation**\n","\n","Offline evaluation means testing your AI application using a predefined dataset before or outside live production traffic.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","- You have 500 test questions.\n","- You change the prompt.\n","- You run the application against all 500 questions.\n","- You compare the results.\n","\n","It answers:\n","\n","> Is the new version better than the old version?\n","\n","**Online evaluation**\n","\n","Online evaluation means evaluating real application executions as users interact with the deployed system.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","- Your chatbot receives actual user queries.\n","- LangSmith traces those executions.\n","- Evaluators score relevant production runs.\n","- You analyze quality degradation or unusual patterns.\n","\n","It answers:\n","\n","> Is my deployed application performing well with real users?\n","\n","![Dataset Evaluation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/langsmith_dataset_evaluation.png)\n","\n","## Production monitoring\n","\n","Tracing and evaluation are not limited to development. \n","\n","### Latency\n","\n","Latency means the time required to complete a request.\n","\n","Example:\n","\n","| Operation           | Latency  |\n","| ------------------- | -------- |\n","| Embedding           | 100 ms   |\n","| FAISS search        | 20 ms    |\n","| Prompt construction | 10 ms    |\n","| Gemini API          | 1,500 ms |\n","| Total               | 1,630 ms |\n","\n","The LLM is the main bottleneck in this example.\n","\n","Useful metrics:\n","\n","- Average latency.\n","- P50 latency.\n","- P95 latency.\n","- P99 latency.\n","\n","Why P95?\n","\n","Suppose 95% of requests complete within 2 seconds, but the remaining 5% take 10 seconds.\n","\n","Average latency might hide that problem. P95 gives a better understanding of the slower requests.\n","\n","### Token usage\n","\n","Track:\n","\n","- Input tokens.\n","- Output tokens.\n","- Total tokens.\n","\n","More tokens often increase cost and latency.\n","\n","### Cost\n","\n","Monitor model usage and estimated cost by:\n","\n","- Project.\n","- Model.\n","- Request.\n","- Environment.\n","- User group, where appropriate.\n","\n","### Errors\n","\n","Track:\n","\n","- Rate limit errors.\n","- API failures.\n","- Timeouts.\n","- Invalid model outputs.\n","- Tool errors.\n","- Retrieval failures.\n","\n","### Quality\n","\n","Monitor evaluation scores and user feedback.\n","\n","An application can be technically healthy but produce poor answers. This is why AI observability is different from ordinary infrastructure monitoring.\n","\n","## Advanced Concepts\n","\n","\n","### CI/CD integration\n","\n","You can run evaluations during software development.\n","\n","Example workflow:\n","\n","![CI/CD Workflow](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/langsmith_ci_cd.png)\n","\n","For example, you might require:\n","\n","```\n","minimum_accuracy = 0.90\n","```\n","\n","If the evaluation score falls below your quality threshold, the deployment can be blocked.\n","\n","The exact CI/CD implementation depends on your SDK version and how you configure the evaluation pipeline.\n","\n","## LangSmith vs MLflow vs Langfuse\n","\n","| Feature                    | LangSmith               | MLflow    | Langfuse              |\n","| -------------------------- | ----------------------- | --------- | --------------------- |\n","| LLM tracing                | Yes                     | Yes       | Yes                   |\n","| LLM evaluation             | Yes                     | Yes       | Yes                   |\n","| Datasets                   | Yes                     | Yes       | Yes                   |\n","| Prompt management          | Yes                     | Yes       | Yes                   |\n","| Agent tracing              | Strong                  | Supported | Supported             |\n","| LangChain integration      | Native                  | Supported | Supported             |\n","| Open-source self-hosting   | Deployment options vary | Yes       | Yes                   |\n","| ML model lifecycle         | Not its primary focus   | Strong    | Not its primary focus |\n","| LLM-specific observability | Strong                  | Yes       | Strong                |\n","\n","The best tool depends on your project.\n","\n","- Choose LangSmith if you are building LangChain or LangGraph applications and want integrated tracing and evaluation.\n","- Choose MLflow if you need broader ML experiment tracking, model lifecycle management, and LLM features.\n","- Choose Langfuse if you want an open-source-oriented LLM observability stack.\n","\n","These tools are not mutually exclusive.\n","\n","\n","## Security\n","\n","When you trace an application, the recorded inputs and outputs may contain sensitive data.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```json\n","{    \n","    \"user_email\": \"user@example.com\",    \n","    \"question\": \"My bank account information is...\"\n","}\n","```\n","\n","This could be recorded in a trace if you instrument the relevant code.\n","\n","Therefore:\n","\n","- Avoid sending passwords, API keys, or secrets to traces.\n","- Mask sensitive information where appropriate.\n","- Avoid tracing unnecessary personal information.\n","- Configure access permissions carefully.\n","- Understand your organization's data retention and data residency requirements.\n","- Use appropriate self-hosted or managed deployment options for your security needs.\n","\n","LangSmith provides managed and enterprise deployment options, including self-hosting and bring-your-own-cloud offerings.\n","\n","## Interview Questions\n","\n","<details>\n","\n","<summary>What is LangSmith?</summary>\n","\n","LangSmith is a platform for developing, debugging, evaluating, and monitoring LLM applications and AI agents. It provides tracing, evaluation datasets, experiments, human feedback, and production observability.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is the difference between LangChain and LangSmith?</summary>\n","\n","LangChain is used to build LLM applications. LangSmith is used to trace, debug, evaluate, and monitor those applications.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is tracing?</summary>\n","\n","Tracing is the process of recording an application's execution steps, including inputs, outputs, intermediate operations, and timing information.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is a run?</summary>\n","\n","A run is one execution of a component, such as an LLM call, retrieval function, tool invocation, or chain.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is a trace?</summary>\n","\n","A trace is a hierarchical record of the execution associated with a request. It can contain multiple nested runs.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is a dataset in LangSmith?</summary>\n","\n","A dataset is a collection of examples used to benchmark and evaluate an AI application.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>What is an experiment?</summary>\n","\n","An experiment is the result of running a particular application configuration against a dataset, including outputs, traces, and evaluator scores.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>How do you evaluate an AI agent?</summary>\n","\n","I would evaluate:\n","\n","- Task completion.\n","- Tool selection accuracy.\n","- Tool argument correctness.\n","- Execution trajectory.\n","- Final response correctness.\n","- Efficiency and unnecessary tool calls.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>How would you use LangSmith in CI/CD?</summary>\n","\n","I would run a benchmark dataset after changes to prompts, models, or application logic. If evaluation metrics fall below an acceptable threshold, I would fail the pipeline and prevent deployment.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>Can LangSmith work without LangChain?</summary>\n","\n","Yes. LangSmith is framework-agnostic and supports tracing and evaluation for custom applications and other LLM frameworks.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>Does LangSmith prevent hallucinations?</summary>\n","\n","No. LangSmith helps detect, investigate, measure, and monitor hallucinations. Preventing or reducing them requires improvements to prompts, retrieval, models, and application logic.\n","\n","</details>\n","\n","<details>\n","<summary>How would you monitor an LLM application in production?</summary>\n","\n","I would monitor latency, errors, token usage, cost, evaluation scores, user feedback, and agent execution patterns. I would configure alerts for important failures or quality degradation.\n","\n","</details>"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":35,"id":"f2322e44","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.324347Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.323828Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.329532Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.328521Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019763,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.331441+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.311678+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["PRODUCTS = {\n","    \"P001\": {\n","        \"id\": \"P001\",\n","        \"name\": \"Laptop\",\n","        \"price\": 1200,\n","        \"stock\": 10\n","    },\n","    \"P002\": {\n","        \"id\": \"P002\",\n","        \"name\": \"Mouse\",\n","        \"price\": 25,\n","        \"stock\": 100\n","    },\n","    \"P003\": {\n","        \"id\": \"P003\",\n","        \"name\": \"Keyboard\",\n","        \"price\": 50,\n","        \"stock\": 40\n","    }\n","}"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":36,"id":"a0d9f1fa","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.353841Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.352591Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.359343Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.358249Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02053,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.361801+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.341271+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def get_product(product_id: str):\n","    product = PRODUCTS.get(product_id)\n","\n","    if product is None:\n","        return {\n","            \"error\": \"Product not found\"\n","        }\n","\n","    return product"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":37,"id":"ff7d86e7","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.384698Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.383623Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.389703Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.388462Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.0198,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.391849+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.372049+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def search_products(query: str):\n","    query = query.lower()\n","\n","    results = [\n","        product\n","        for product in PRODUCTS.values()\n","        if query in product[\"name\"].lower()\n","    ]\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"results\": results\n","    }"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":38,"id":"fb261752","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.413706Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.413036Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.419348Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.418214Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019661,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.421395+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.401734+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def calculate_total(\n","    price: float,\n","    quantity: int\n","):\n","    if price < 0 or quantity < 0:\n","        return {\n","            \"error\": \"Price and quantity must be non-negative\"\n","        }\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"price\": price,\n","        \"quantity\": quantity,\n","        \"total\": price * quantity\n","    }"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"56585f1e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009421,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.440433+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.431012+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Tool Calling\n","\n","Tool calling is a capability that allows a Large Language Model (LLM) to request the execution of an external function, API, database query, or another operation to accomplish a task.\n","\n","An LLM by itself primarily generates text. It cannot directly:\n","\n","- Query your MongoDB database.\n","- Read live weather information.\n","- Send an email.\n","- Execute a Python function in your application.\n","- Access a private API.\n","- Retrieve live stock prices.\n","\n","Tool calling enables the LLM to request that your application perform these actions.\n","\n","**Important:** The LLM does not necessarily execute the function itself. It generates a structured tool-call request. Your application or agent runtime executes the actual function.\n","\n","## Tool Calling vs Function Calling\n","\n","These terms are often used interchangeably.\n","\n","| Concept          | Meaning                                                     |\n","| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n","| Tool calling     | General concept of an LLM requesting an external capability |\n","| Function calling | Tool calling specifically through functions                 |\n","| API calling      | Sending a request to an external API                        |\n","| Database tool    | A tool that interacts with a database                       |\n","| MCP tool         | A tool exposed through the Model Context Protocol           |\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```\n","get_weather(city=\"Dhaka\")\n","```\n","\n","This is a function.\n","\n","* If an LLM decides to invoke this function, it is function calling or tool calling.\n","* If the function uses an external weather API internally, then it also performs an API call.\n","\n","## Process\n","\n","The LLM does not magically understand Python functions or directly execute your code.\n","\n","Let's understand how it decides to call a tool.\n","\n","### Tool Definition\n","\n","You provide the LLM with a description of the tools."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":39,"id":"1589358d","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.463586Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.463154Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.470171Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.468939Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.021635,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.472093+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.450458+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["\n","TOOLS = [\n","    {\n","        \"type\": \"function\",\n","        \"function\": {\n","            \"name\": \"get_product\",\n","            \"description\": \"Retrieve product details using its product ID.\",\n","            \"parameters\": {\n","                \"type\": \"object\",\n","                \"properties\": {\n","                    \"product_id\": {\n","                        \"type\": \"string\",\n","                        \"description\": \"The product ID\"\n","                    }\n","                },\n","                \"required\": [\"product_id\"],\n","                \"additionalProperties\": False\n","            },\n","            \"strict\": True\n","        }\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"type\": \"function\",\n","        \"function\": {\n","            \"name\": \"calculate_total\",\n","            \"description\": \"Calculate total price from unit price and quantity.\",\n","            \"parameters\": {\n","                \"type\": \"object\",\n","                \"properties\": {\n","                    \"price\": {\n","                        \"type\": \"number\"\n","                    },\n","                    \"quantity\": {\n","                        \"type\": \"integer\"\n","                    }\n","                },\n","                \"required\": [\"price\", \"quantity\"],\n","                \"additionalProperties\": False\n","            },\n","            \"strict\": True\n","        }\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"type\": \"function\",\n","        \"function\": {\n","            \"name\": \"search_products\",\n","            \"description\": \"Search the product catalog by product name.\",\n","            \"parameters\": {\n","                \"type\": \"object\",\n","                \"properties\": {\n","                    \"query\": {\n","                        \"type\": \"string\"\n","                    }\n","                },\n","                \"required\": [\"query\"],\n","                \"additionalProperties\": False\n","            },\n","            \"strict\": True\n","        }\n","    }\n","]\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"59386a70","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.009486,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.491323+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.481837+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["\n","The model receives:\n","\n","- Tool name\n","- Tool description\n","- Argument names\n","- Argument types\n","- Required arguments\n","- Schema constraints\n","\n","The tool definition acts like a contract between the model and your application.\n","\n","**Understanding the schema**\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```json\n","\"parameters\": {\n","    \"type\": \"object\",\n","    \"properties\": {\n","        \"product_id\": {\n","            \"type\": \"string\"\n","        }\n","    },\n","    \"required\": [\"product_id\"],\n","    \"additionalProperties\": False\n","}\n","```\n","\n","This tells the model:\n","\n","- Arguments must be an object.\n","- The object has a `product_id` property.\n","- The value must be a string.\n","- `product_id` is required.\n","- Additional properties are prohibited.\n","\n","The `strict: True` setting asks the API to enforce supported schema constraints on the generated arguments. It does not validate permissions, business logic, or whether the product ID exists.&#x20;\n","\n","### Model Output\n","\n","When the user says: `What is the weather in Dhaka?` The model determines that `get_weather` is appropriate.\n","\n","Conceptually, the model generates a special structured output representing a function call."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":40,"id":"cd2ea15a","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.512736Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.511792Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.516932Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.516029Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.018071,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.518912+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.500841+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["user_input = \"Find laptop\""]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":41,"id":"47cf95e5","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.540333Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.539938Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.545688Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.544521Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.019452,"end_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.547951+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-20T12:25:29.528499+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["messages = [\n","        {\n","            \"r